Saa WILL TO GO mirai he to PLAY ON!

02:05.790 --> 02:06.660
It's finished,

02:07.750 --> 02:12.710
Registration for Cycling Club

02:08.710 --> 02:12.880
my and Fukazawa-san's bright future.

02:52.880 --> 02:54.590
Umm... What's up?

02:55.000 --> 02:57.800
What's your relationship with Fukazawa-san?

03:00.510 --> 03:02.970
Umm... We don't really have anything special...

03:03.140 --> 03:08.560
Just...

03:08.810 --> 03:09.600
No such thing.

03:11.480 --> 03:13.480
Are you looking down on me?

03:13.650 --> 03:18.570
Sorry. Just let him punch you. This guys' interested in Fukazawa.

03:18.690 --> 03:20.940
Sh-Shut up, idiot!

03:21.150 --> 03:22.490
And...

03:24.530 --> 03:28.830
I just saved the drowning Fukazawa-san.

03:29.200 --> 03:32.160
Actually, he was the one who was saved

03:32.870 --> 03:36.080
Who cares!

03:47.180 --> 03:50.930
This should be Yuki's class.

03:51.730 --> 03:53.640
Where? Where is tiny?

03:55.060 --> 03:56.980
Yousuke-san appeared!

03:58.520 --> 04:00.480
What? Is he a student from our school?

04:00.740 --> 04:02.110
Isn't he dangerous?

04:02.490 --> 04:03.490
But he's so cool.

04:04.110 --> 04:08.080
Don't you know? He's really famous.

04:16.710 --> 04:19.840
Here you are, tiny.

04:22.800 --> 04:25.130
I came to get the club registration application.

04:30.140 --> 04:34.850
What was that noise just now?

04:35.020 --> 04:36.730
It's Shinozaki!

04:38.400 --> 04:42.990
I didn't do this.

04:43.490 --> 04:44.610
‌‌Huh?

04:50.740 --> 04:55.210
First, clean up the glass.

04:55.620 --> 04:56.960
It's Shinozaki.

05:02.840 --> 05:04.460
What's he doing?

05:20.940 --> 05:23.480
New... New member?

05:23.990 --> 05:27.320
Yep. Amazing, right? I was the one who found him.

05:28.320 --> 05:31.780
This is Terao Kouichi, Yousuke's childhood friend.

05:32.120 --> 05:36.750
He's supposed to be the one bullied, but because there are only two members here,

05:37.620 --> 05:40.080
When we were little, I also used to pick on him a lot.

05:40.920 --> 05:43.630
Okay, Shinozaki, give a greeting.

05:43.630 --> 05:48.760
Umm... Shinozaki was a name my dad found

05:49.340 --> 05:53.760
‌‌randomly flipping through the dictionary.

05:54.270 --> 06:00.850
A-And... I just learned how to ride a bicycle not too long ago.

06:01.520 --> 06:12.910
Specifically, I only learned it in two days.

06:15.750 --> 06:18.750
I'm so sorry!

06:21.460 --> 06:23.090
Why are you apologizing?

06:24.170 --> 06:26.670
All right, all right. Just don't do it again.

06:28.090 --> 06:29.840
Idiot 1

06:29.130 --> 06:29.930
Idiot 2

06:29.220 --> 06:29.890
Is he as well?

06:31.470 --> 06:32.720
B-But, he's cute.

06:33.600 --> 06:34.550
This guy, too?

06:36.970 --> 06:42.310
Finally in my third year, I got a junior.

06:42.810 --> 06:44.730
Don't worry. I'll protect you from getting poisoned by Yousuke, okay?

06:47.610 --> 06:49.950
I'm welcomed.

06:50.660 --> 06:55.780
But what does the Bicycle Club do anyway?

06:57.040 --> 07:02.420
Fukazawa-san, that would be... You see... Umm... You see... You see... Umm...

07:02.960 --> 07:03.420
What?

07:06.590 --> 07:11.630
Umm... The Bicycle Club goes cycling in the wild, of course.

07:13.140 --> 07:14.470
Wait for me.

07:14.550 --> 07:15.350
Hurry and catch up.

07:18.140 --> 07:20.890
Right, right? Terao-san, what I said is like that, right?

07:21.230 --> 07:23.690
Fukazawa-san is really...

07:24.480 --> 07:28.150
Shinozaki, that brat immediately gets excited because he's made some friends.

07:29.240 --> 07:32.650
No, no. Our club isn't like that.

07:32.910 --> 07:34.700
So it's a track race.

07:34.910 --> 07:37.370
No, no It's still cycling, right?

07:45.380 --> 07:47.540
The bicycle represents freedom.

07:55.260 --> 07:59.640
Freedom? I understand.

08:00.060 --> 08:02.310
You don't understand it at all.

08:06.480 --> 08:13.650
Isn't that Shinozaki? That inconspicuous guy in class? He looks weird.

08:28.380 --> 08:29.540
Road race?

08:30.130 --> 08:35.720
That's right. There are many types of bicycle races,

08:36.180 --> 08:37.890
Is it different from a track race?

08:38.640 --> 08:42.350
A track race is at a set place, circling around the track.

08:43.730 --> 08:45.770
A road race is on the everyday road.

08:46.600 --> 08:50.400
Road? Which road?

08:51.150 --> 08:51.980
Anywhere is fine.

08:53.530 --> 08:56.240
The mountain, riverside, and even the desert.

08:56.950 --> 09:00.780
In other words, the whole world is your battlefield.

09:03.250 --> 09:08.120
Battlefield? The whole world is my battlefield?

09:14.090 --> 09:15.840
Wait, Shinozaki-kun.

09:16.470 --> 09:17.970
I can do it.

09:19.930 --> 09:25.480
I'll definitely be okay.

09:38.490 --> 09:39.610
You brat!

09:43.700 --> 09:45.450
Hurry and run away from the scene!

09:46.370 --> 09:48.460
Stop right there!

09:51.130 --> 09:54.420
Listen well, Shinozaki-kun. You must carefully look ahead.

09:55.300 --> 09:56.720
A bicycle and a car are the same.

09:57.430 --> 09:59.220
You must stop at the signals.

10:04.100 --> 10:04.640
Are you listening?

10:08.810 --> 10:12.650
Okay. I can! I can do it!

10:13.320 --> 10:17.030
He's not listening, but first-years are cute.

10:17.610 --> 10:19.740
Every child must feel like this, too.

10:20.450 --> 10:22.570
No, that guy is just a bit weird.

10:23.240 --> 10:26.750
But Shinozaki-kun is not suited to ride a bicycle.

10:29.920 --> 10:35.420
He isn't tall, his muscles are not firm,

10:39.220 --> 10:42.180
Although the most important part i the spirit...

10:46.640 --> 10:49.390
Oh well. He's cute, so I'm fine with it.

10:51.020 --> 10:55.860
Huh? He seems completely useless just by standing...

10:57.150 --> 10:58.320
I-I'm sorry.

10:59.650 --> 11:02.820
But after riding on the bicycle, he seems to have an impression.

11:03.990 --> 11:08.830
The bicycle looks a bit too big.

11:10.000 --> 11:13.580
To be able to successfully step on the pedals, is it because his muscles are flexible?

11:14.790 --> 11:18.460
All this must be the lack of ability in Japanese people.

11:22.930 --> 11:25.260
Shinozaki-kun, which is your dominant leg?

11:28.180 --> 11:30.520
Like which leg do you kick the soccer ball with?

11:31.600 --> 11:33.810
Each leg is the same.

11:35.400 --> 11:40.190
But it's too bad, I've never been able to kick the ball into the goal.

11:40.570 --> 11:41.570
Both legs?

11:43.320 --> 11:43.990
What about eyesight?

11:44.530 --> 11:47.450
Probably about 2.0 ...

11:47.950 --> 11:51.580
2.0? Now?

11:54.250 --> 11:56.460
Th-This kid... Has perfect eyesight?

11:57.460 --> 12:00.090
He's a bicycle God!

12:00.720 --> 12:02.130
Terao-san is weird.

12:03.590 --> 12:05.510
No. I can't make a decision yet.

12:09.770 --> 12:12.930
Could it be that Yousuke's already noticed this?

12:14.690 --> 12:16.310
In other words, he really...

12:19.440 --> 12:21.030
Calm down, Terao Kouichi.

12:22.700 --> 12:26.610
Whether or not he has perfect eyesight, the aspect of muscle tone is very important.

12:27.530 --> 12:30.580
Spirit, Yousuke and I can slowly foster.

12:32.200 --> 12:36.080
If the training goes well, this kid might be able to change completely.

12:40.000 --> 12:41.340
He really is weird.

12:42.760 --> 12:43.880
Even so...

12:52.390 --> 12:55.140
Yousuke, isn't this a bit too fast?

12:57.060 --> 12:58.980
To start off at this speed is not good.

13:00.730 --> 13:03.740
It's going to be dangerous if you don't slow down.

13:07.990 --> 13:09.660
I can't see the front.

13:10.620 --> 13:14.330
Are you okay, Shinozaki-kun? Have your leg muscles become sore?

13:25.930 --> 13:27.220
What was that?

13:28.890 --> 13:30.260
Did I hit something?

13:31.600 --> 13:36.430
Wall?

13:37.850 --> 13:43.780
Shinozaki-kun! Shinozaki-kun!

13:45.240 --> 13:49.700
Not good. That's why I said, Yousuke, you were too fast.

13:50.830 --> 13:57.370
Suddenly riding at 50 km/h,

13:57.960 --> 13:59.500
Yeah. Sorry.

13:59.960 --> 14:05.260
What "Sorry"? This kid might never want to ride again.

14:06.670 --> 14:10.180
You understand, don't you? If his heart is planted with fear, it's not easy to erase it.

14:14.470 --> 14:21.440
After this, he'll definitely hate bicycles.

14:24.900 --> 14:26.230
What are you doing?

14:26.780 --> 14:27.820
Praying.

14:33.700 --> 14:34.530
Interesting.

14:39.500 --> 14:42.750
"Interesting"? You just fell.

14:43.210 --> 14:45.090
Bicycles are really interesting.

14:45.630 --> 14:46.590
Doesn't it hurt?

14:47.170 --> 14:50.010
What are you talking about? Of course it hurts.

14:50.930 --> 14:55.560
But you definitely don't experience this in everyday life.

14:56.520 --> 14:58.640
Anyhow, you should go to the hospital.

14:59.520 --> 15:01.310
No need. It's completely fine.

15:02.400 --> 15:03.270
Let's continue.

15:04.060 --> 15:05.230
To where?

15:05.900 --> 15:08.780
Really. Of course it's to continue riding.

15:16.240 --> 15:18.200
To this day, I can still clearly remember.

15:19.790 --> 15:23.040
My second year, my first falling accident.

15:24.540 --> 15:28.630
My clothes were torn, my skin was rubbed raw, and the bicycle broke, unable to ride.

15:29.970 --> 15:35.800
Of course, I didn't depend upon the bicycle to make a living, so I quit.

15:36.760 --> 15:43.650
That accident left me a painful memory.

15:45.190 --> 15:49.030
But how can you still ride under this circumstance?

15:50.320 --> 15:56.910
Although the wound on his head isn't deep,

15:58.290 --> 16:02.830
He's obviously reached his limit,

16:04.040 --> 16:07.070
He's different from Yousuke, and of course different from me.

16:07.110 --> 16:09.800
I've never seen this kind of road racer.

16:29.980 --> 16:32.820
Before today, there has never been something that made me so happy.

16:33.610 --> 16:35.490
My heart has never jumped like this before.

16:36.910 --> 16:40.950
Until now, the world I've never arrived at is here.

16:41.830 --> 16:44.540
This is it. Pure happiness.

16:55.970 --> 16:58.050
After this hill, let's turn back.

17:00.010 --> 17:05.940
I keep feeling like it's dangerous when that kid is on a bicycle.

17:07.440 --> 17:08.600
Dangerous?

17:09.730 --> 17:10.440
But...

17:14.030 --> 17:14.990
Interesting.

17:23.290 --> 17:25.290
I couldn't keep up at all.

17:27.750 --> 17:32.550
Damn it! What's wrong with these legs?

17:33.630 --> 17:36.670
I can still ride. I can still run!

17:39.510 --> 17:40.850
You're not qualified.

17:44.930 --> 17:45.680
Shinozaki-kun.

17:48.650 --> 17:49.650
No!

17:50.730 --> 17:53.400
I'm saying, if today was a race.

17:54.860 --> 17:57.990
Ow.

17:58.990 --> 18:02.030
Do you understand now? The rules are simple.

18:03.290 --> 18:08.040
The person who rides the fastest to the finish line wins. Those who are too slow are not qualified.

18:09.040 --> 18:13.790
He might fall in the middle, and he might also get hurt. The circumstances are dangerous, the surroundings are full of enemies.

18:15.290 --> 18:17.420
Even so, there can only be one winner.

18:18.630 --> 18:25.390
After understanding this, can you still swear to continue?

18:27.940 --> 18:33.520
I can do it. I don't need to give up. I can ride the bicycle.

18:34.440 --> 18:36.360
Seems like he really does want to ride the bicycle.

18:39.320 --> 18:45.160
Similarly,

18:45.700 --> 18:46.620
Kill?

18:46.910 --> 18:48.500
One month later? That's too fast!

18:49.620 --> 18:52.540
Listen well. Cycling is a team play.

18:53.170 --> 18:57.170
It depends upon the situation to determine who's the ace and who's the assistant.

18:58.130 --> 19:02.220
Just picking one is fine.

19:03.470 --> 19:09.930
No, surpass us in ability,

19:11.850 --> 19:12.690
Team?

19:13.690 --> 19:14.520
What?

19:22.910 --> 19:25.410
Team? What's a team?

19:26.410 --> 19:29.660
Is it comrades? Friends?

19:31.370 --> 19:32.920
You did it, congratulations.

19:33.630 --> 19:34.580
You can succeed if you do it.

19:36.340 --> 19:41.920
That's not it. I didn't do anything today.

19:44.800 --> 19:47.510
Fukazawa-san! Why are you here...

19:47.600 --> 19:50.600
How was it? Are you a little more like him now?

19:53.440 --> 19:54.770
Of course.

19:56.690 --> 20:01.150
Yousuke was this small when he began riding a bicycle.

20:01.740 --> 20:05.450
How can someone like you, who just began, be like him?

20:06.580 --> 20:09.290
If you put it like that, I can't argue.

20:09.790 --> 20:11.700
And also, that expression just now.

20:13.170 --> 20:19.130
When you ran the relays in middle school, you always had an apathetic look.

20:20.670 --> 20:28.430
But if just a bicycle can make you let out and expression like that, then isn't that...

20:29.060 --> 20:31.350
Come on,

20:31.480 --> 20:32.680
come on.

20:37.150 --> 20:38.110
Guess I won't say it.

20:41.570 --> 20:44.070
You've been getting cocky lately.

20:44.400 --> 20:45.990
No, no.

20:46.200 --> 20:51.990
My only good point is I'm not an arrogant person. Haven't I always lived a modest life?

20:53.710 --> 20:57.630
Three hours, 25 minutes.

20:58.170 --> 20:59.170
Unexpectedly quick.

21:00.130 --> 21:00.750
Right?

21:01.090 --> 21:04.260
And his gears are always shifted to the heaviest level.

21:06.800 --> 21:10.260
His hand grip is on the low level.

21:11.520 --> 21:12.970
Everything would give both legs too much strain.

21:14.100 --> 21:18.100
Yuki said he, until now, has never participated in any sport.

21:19.690 --> 21:21.070
Could he be a genius?

21:21.860 --> 21:32.700
Although his form is different, he's like some sort of battle person,

21:39.460 --> 21:41.790
Not good! It's been a long time since I was fired up.

21:42.380 --> 21:45.550
Enough warm-ups. Time for the second stage.

22:07.900 --> 22:12.190
Kaze ga toorisugiteku

22:08.400 --> 22:12.690
The wind glides by,

22:13.280 --> 22:17.200
Karada wo surinukete

22:13.280 --> 22:17.200
Brushing against our body.

22:17.530 --> 22:22.990
Itsushika iro ase bokete shimatta

22:17.530 --> 22:22.990
The colors faded in the farthest end of the sky,

22:23.040 --> 22:27.120
Sora no saihate de

22:23.040 --> 22:27.120
before we realized.

22:28.170 --> 22:36.170
Nama atatakai kaze ga fuiteru fuiteru

22:28.170 --> 22:36.170
The luke warm breeze is blowing, blowing.

22:37.800 --> 22:41.600
Mujun darake no sekai de

22:37.800 --> 22:41.600
In a world full on inconsistency,

22:41.720 --> 22:47.430
Toke sou no kimi ga futto boku ni waraikaketa

22:41.720 --> 22:47.430
Melting into it, you grin at me with a whiff.

22:56.360 --> 23:00.950
Kaze ga toorisugiteku

22:56.360 --> 23:00.950
The wind glides by,

23:01.200 --> 23:04.830
Karada wo surinukete

23:01.200 --> 23:04.830
Brushing against our body.

23:05.410 --> 23:10.920
Itsushika a iro ase bokete shimatta

23:05.410 --> 23:10.920
The colors faded before we realized.

23:11.000 --> 23:20.130
Sora no saihate de aou

23:11.000 --> 23:20.130
Let's meet at the furthest end of the sky.
